From: j7
Subject: j7: build the panel row once, and paint every dark pixel

The frame now holds 9 fps with the tearing gone and cpu_mhz=891, and the cost is all in the
row build: 65 ms of a 106 ms frame, which is 45 ns for a source pixel that is one uncached read
of the client's surface.  memcpy each source row into cacheable memory once and build from there,
and do the same for the wallpaper sample, whose column is now a table built once per present.

The wallpaper itself still never appeared because the paint required a run of 32 output pixels of
the same colour, and at 1.44x one source pixel covers one or two, so that test could not match on
this panel.  Paint every dark opaque pixel with the picture instead.

Co-Authored-By: dipa-studio <183933817+dipa-studio@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -1080,29 +1080,39 @@
 
 /*
  * The picture is the logical display size and a swap record's layer is whatever the client says,
- * not always the same size: requiring an exact match meant no wallpaper was ever sampled (the
- * log said "took 0 background pixels" on a frame whose dominant colour was black).  Sample the
- * picture at the layer's pixel position instead, nearest neighbour.
+ * not always the same size, so the picture is sampled at the layer's own pixel position, nearest
+ * neighbour.  The row of the picture is the same for every pixel of a logical row and the column
+ * is the same for every output pixel of a source column, so the two halves are split: the column
+ * table is built once per present, and the caller keeps a pointer to the picture's row.
  */
-static inline uint32_t
-sweet_fb_wall_at(int32_t c, int32_t r, int32_t w, int32_t h)
+static inline uint16_t
+sweet_fb_wall_col(int32_t c, int32_t w)
 {
-	if (sweet_fb_wall == NULL || sweet_fb_wall_w <= 0 || sweet_fb_wall_h <= 0 || w <= 0 || h <= 0) {
+	if (sweet_fb_wall == NULL || sweet_fb_wall_w <= 0 || w <= 0) {
 		return 0;
 	}
 	int64_t sx = (int64_t)c * sweet_fb_wall_w / w;
-	int64_t sy = (int64_t)r * sweet_fb_wall_h / h;
 	if (sx < 0) {
 		sx = 0;
 	} else if (sx >= sweet_fb_wall_w) {
 		sx = sweet_fb_wall_w - 1;
 	}
+	return (uint16_t)sx;
+}
+
+static inline const uint32_t *
+sweet_fb_wall_row(int32_t r, int32_t h)
+{
+	if (sweet_fb_wall == NULL || sweet_fb_wall_w <= 0 || sweet_fb_wall_h <= 0 || h <= 0) {
+		return NULL;
+	}
+	int64_t sy = (int64_t)r * sweet_fb_wall_h / h;
 	if (sy < 0) {
 		sy = 0;
 	} else if (sy >= sweet_fb_wall_h) {
 		sy = sweet_fb_wall_h - 1;
 	}
-	return sweet_fb_wall[(uint64_t)sy * (uint64_t)sweet_fb_wall_w + (uint64_t)sx];
+	return sweet_fb_wall + (uint64_t)sy * (uint64_t)sweet_fb_wall_w;
 }
 
 
